course: dictionary
lesson: 5106
title: Words that change languages
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An interpreter is a person who changes what someone says into another language, out loud, as they speak. «Sign language interpreters translate live between spoken language and sign language, so Deaf people can follow things like the news.» Live means as it happens, with no time to write it down first.
explain: The same word has other meanings. In computing, an interpreter is a program that reads code line by line and runs it. «A compiler or interpreter translates code written in a language like Rust or Python into machine code, the 1s and 0s the processor runs.» Which meaning fits? Read the words around it, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check.
explain: A third meaning is a person who explains what something means. Joseph in the Bible was an interpreter of dreams, because he explained what dreams meant. When you meet interpreter, look at the clues: is it about people talking, a computer, or explaining?
fact: An interpreter is a person whose job is to change speech from one language into another, as it is said.
fact: «Through an interpreter» means talking across two languages with the help of someone who changes the words for you.
fact: «Interpreters turn one into the other as they talk» in Canada's Parliament in Ottawa, because MPs speak English or French.
fact: Canada has two official languages, English and French, and its laws are written in both.
fact: In computing, an interpreter reads and runs code line by line, and Python uses an interpreter.
exercise: «Sign language interpreters translate live between spoken language and sign language, so Deaf people can follow the news.» What does an interpreter do here? | *Changes speech into sign language as it happens | Writes the news down in a book for later | Reads the news aloud on the radio | Teaches sign language to school children
exercise: In Ottawa, «interpreters turn one into the other as they talk.» What does interpreter mean here? | A politician who makes laws | *A person who changes speech from one language into another | A person who writes letters | A computer program that runs code
exercise: In computing, what does an interpreter do? | Sends emails to other computers | Draws pictures on the screen | Stores photos in a album | *Reads and runs code line by line
test: Joseph in the Bible explained the meaning of dreams. Which meaning of interpreter fits this? | A person who changes speech into another language | *A person who explains what something means | A computer program that runs code
test: «Canada has two official languages, English and French; interpreters translate as they speak.» What are Canada's two official languages? | Welsh and Scots | *English and French | Hindi and Urdu | Spanish and German
exam: What does «through an interpreter» mean? | *A talk held across two languages, with someone who changes the words as they are spoken | A talk held in complete silence | A talk held on a computer screen only | A talk held in a church
